Z||000000||SLYGUY||09-27-2001||03:57 AM||||Anyone know where I could get a hold of the plastic tube that runs from the EGR solenoid, under the intake, and routes to the EGR vacuum port?<P>I replaced the EGR with a 'universal' one and broke the tube in the process. Tube broke.<P>Sly||||reg||8
Z||000001||Haagster||09-27-2001||05:21 AM||||Instead of the plastic ones, consider spending a little extra for metal...  You can get the whole set at <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  (I haven't gotten them myself, but they are on my list of things to do, soon)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-27-2001||08:28 AM||||I call that black vinyl tubing "blackaroni," because it looks like black macaroni - and of course, it snaps just as easily.  Especially after it ages and gets brittle.<P>If it hasn't broken into a dozen pieces (and if you didn't get mad and throw it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ), you can splice the breaks using short pieces of small-diameter flexible rubber vacuum line or windshield washer hose.  That's what I have done in the past, and it works just fine.<P>That'll get you going until Rodney's steel lines arrive  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||09-27-2001||09:10 AM||||Most auto parts store will carry it. There's a brand something like O-Lite or ending like that which sells a 3' piece for less than $3. I just bought some two days ago. Put it in boilung water for 1-2 minutes to get the memory-bending out of it (stretch it). Otherwise it will be harded to route.||||reg||1
